<p>President Trump said Friday that U.S. naval enforcement of Washington’s blockade of Iranian ports resembled piracy during the U.S. and Israel’s war against Iran, describing recent ship-and-oil seizures as “a very profitable business”. Speaking at the Forum Club of the Palm Beaches in Florida, Trump said U.S. forces had taken control of a vessel, its cargo and its oil, and said the operations were meant as a serious warning. The remarks followed U.S. operations against vessels linked to Iran around Iranian ports, the Strait of Hormuz and Asian waters. Iran has blocked nearly all ships passing through the Strait of Hormuz apart from its own since the start of the war, and Trump has imposed a separate blockade on Iranian ports. The U.S. and Israel attacked Iran on February 28, after which Iran launched strikes on Israel and Gulf states hosting U.S. bases.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/qbwKxMhWIe_o-__mSbRCrlbiH2IrvUDzezWv6eNiyO0BWFMYJwXsB9ZEcYaqZ1pdhl3pb8VeOSeKaKgMciAlTCtYK-ao1ekqL1EiZVUD4Q' alt='A view of Iranian-flagged cargo ship M/V Touska as the U.S. Navy guided missile destroyer USS Spruance conducts its interception in the north Arabian Sea.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Audience reaction: RT reported that Trump’s piracy comparison prompted laughter at the Forum Club dinner.</li><li>Iran proposal: Trump said Friday he was not satisfied with Iran’s latest peace proposal, according to reports that also described talks being conducted by phone.</li><li>Legal status: FAZ’s liveblog said the U.S. government declared the war over “in the sense of the law”.</li></ul><blockquote>We&#x27;re like pirates. We&#x27;re sort of like pirates but we are not playing games. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: In the same Florida speech, Trump referred to the Iran war and used the phrase “finish the job,” with Nettavisen reporting that he joked about “taking over” Cuba after U.S. forces return from the conflict. (<a